00:02:41.656 --> 00:02:49.076
Cryo-electron microscopy structures on BioRXIV show how the enzyme RTCB2 repairs damaged ribosomes

00:02:49.076 --> 00:02:56.796
in E. coli after ribotoxin attack. RTCB2 stabilizes the ribosomal head of the damaged 30S subunit.

00:02:57.296 --> 00:03:02.416
It positions the cleaved 3 prime phosphates so the brake can be processed. It then transfers

00:03:02.416 --> 00:03:06.336
