00:03:06.956 --> 00:03:11.716
That sequence is a direct look at ribosomal quality control after RNA cleavage.

00:03:12.575 --> 00:03:17.675
An international team from the University of Plymouth, University College London, the

00:03:17.675 --> 00:03:23.175
University of Washington, and six other institutions published a wildlife hazard framework in nature

00:03:23.175 --> 00:03:27.955
ecology and evolution, treating those harms the way climate assessments treat risk.

00:03:27.955 --> 00:03:34.175
Every year, over 700,000 people die from animal transmitted diseases, snake bites kill

00:03:34.175 --> 00:03:39.555
up to 500,000 people, and crop losses from pests cost around $220 billion.

00:03:40.415 --> 00:03:46.235
The framework treats harm as the intersection of hazards, exposure and vulnerability, mirroring

00:03:46.235 --> 00:03:47.315
IPCC methods.

00:03:47.935 --> 00:03:52.715
Dr. Matthew Faith noted that the structure supports evidence-based policy without prescribing

00:03:52.715 --> 00:03:54.355
specific species management.

00:03:54.355 --> 00:04:00.035
poor healthcare access and socio-economic inequality raise vulnerability to mosquito-borne

00:04:00.035 --> 00:04:05.315
disease, snake bite, and crocodile attacks. The authors call for collaborative management

00:04:05.315 --> 00:04:10.977
with local communities so local knowledge is built into decisions. World Health Organization

00:04:10.977 --> 00:04:15.937
reporting lists heat-health warning systems, climate-resilient drinking water, and sanitation

00:04:15.937 --> 00:04:21.957
infrastructure, improved hand hygiene, cleaner household energy, and efficient fossil fuel pricing

00:04:21.957 --> 00:04:26.877
as measures that could cut 1.6 million deaths, and trillions of dollars in costs.

00:04:27.477 --> 00:04:32.677
Implementation could avoid 16.7 billion tons of carbon dioxide emissions each year.

00:04:33.357 --> 00:04:39.117
The same package could generate up to $5.4 trillion in fiscal benefits annually, plus nearly

00:04:39.117 --> 00:04:44.157
$4 trillion in broader economic gains from saved lives and reduced healthcare costs.

00:04:44.897 --> 00:04:50.657
WHO Director General Tedros Adhanom Ghebriasis stated that scaling proven actions could deliver

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:53.197
the greatest gains in countries that need them most.

00:04:53.777 --> 00:04:57.477
The projections rest on ambitious scenarios with acknowledged data gaps.

