00:07:35.299 --> 00:07:39.959
Most people assume staphilococcus orias stays in the nose because of the microbe itself,

00:07:40.479 --> 00:07:42.279
or because of a person's immune system.

00:07:42.899 --> 00:07:47.899
The surrounding community of nasal bacteria is what allows or blocks long-term colonization.

00:07:48.519 --> 00:07:54.079
Residant species compete for space and nutrients, and some release compounds that inhibit S-Orius

00:07:54.079 --> 00:07:54.459
growth.

00:07:54.979 --> 00:08:00.059
Those contacts, not a solo pathogen trait, sit at the center of who remains a carrier.

00:08:00.059 --> 00:08:04.799
here. Roughly one in three adults carries the bacterium persistently, and the traits

00:08:04.799 --> 00:08:09.639
that sort people into that group are still only partly mapped. Recurrent skin infections

00:08:09.639 --> 00:08:14.539
and mixed results inside a single household track with that community-level filter. The

00:08:14.539 --> 00:08:19.639
next experimental step is to chart those specific microbial contacts so they can be shifted

00:08:19.639 --> 00:08:23.619
